    <div class="container">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            Java is a <b>high-level, object-oriented, and platform-independent</b> programming language. 
            It is widely used for building enterprise-level applications, mobile apps (Android), 
            web applications, and desktop software.
        </p>

        <h2>Key Features of Java</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Platform Independent</b> – Write once, run anywhere (WORA).</li>
            <li><b>Object-Oriented</b> – Supports classes, objects, inheritance, polymorphism, etc.</li>
            <li><b>Robust & Secure</b> – Strong memory management and security features.</li>
            <li><b>Multithreading</b> – Can execute multiple tasks simultaneously.</li>
            <li><b>Rich API</b> – Provides libraries for almost everything.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why Learn Java?</h2>
        <div class="highlight">
            Java is the backbone of many popular technologies such as 
            <b>Spring Framework, Hibernate, Android Development, and Big Data tools (Hadoop)</b>.
        </div>

        <p>
            If you want to build scalable, secure, and performance-oriented applications, 
            then Java is one of the best choices.
        </p>

        <h2>Applications of Java</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Android Mobile Applications</li>
            <li>Web Applications (JSP, Servlets, Spring Boot)</li>
            <li>Enterprise Software (Banking, E-commerce)</li>
            <li>Big Data Processing (Hadoop, Spark)</li>
            <li>Game Development</li>
        </ul>
